# One berth of six is free, and a transport wants two of it.
#
# **This is the weight, and it is why the two sides are separate rows.** The territory holds five
# berths' worth and admits a scout - the test beside this one says so - and refuses a transport,
# which a rule counting vehicles could not tell apart.

{test name:a-transport-takes-two-berths-where-a-scout-takes-one}

{given}
{provides kind:territory what:berth} -> 6
{consumes kind:scout what:berth} -> 1
{consumes kind:transport what:berth} -> 2
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{adjacency id:1 from:territory-1 to:territory-2}
{transport where:territory-1 moving:1} -> 1
{transport where:territory-2 moving:1} -> 2
{scout where:territory-2 moving:1} -> 1

{when}
{move what:transport from:territory-1 to:territory-2}

{refused}
{provides kind:territory what:berth} -> 7
